/A 2243 0 R
/Alt (Three photographic panels compare vibration modalities. Panel \(A\) shows a person in a partial squat on a whole-body vibration platform while holding the support rails. Panel \(B\) shows a handheld focal/localized muscle vibration device with a circular applicator placed against the forearm. Panel \(C\) shows the palm side of a hand wearing a black glove-like support, with a small wired vibrotactile actuator attached at the wrist and highlighted by a red circle. The panels illustrate whole-body vibration, focal/localized muscle vibration, and wearable vibrotactile stimulation, respectively.)
